# Test-drive scratch: the KEY=VALUE file .runcastle/drive-setup.ts writes for the
# server to overlay onto the dev pane. Holds per-drive paths and a port today and
# is the designated home for a connection string tomorrow, so it must never be one
# `git add -A` away from a commit. The scripts themselves ARE tracked — a branch
# that adds a service amends its own drive script.
.runcastle/drive.env

# Claude Code state written into the tree by a spawned agent. `~/` is what an
# unexpanded tilde becomes when a child is spawned without HOME/USERPROFILE — it
# is a literal directory, and one such tree (a 284 KB transcript) was committed
# before the child env was fixed. `.claude/` is the same state under a real home.
~/
.claude/
